Third-party artwork
-------------------

docs/assets/engines/ holds the database logos README shows beside the engines
Ptah supports. Two permissions apply to each file, and they are separate:

  * the SVG file itself, which the icon set below licenses to us; and
  * the mark the file draws, which belongs to the vendor and is not ours to
    license.

The files come from:

  devicons/devicon v2.17.0, MIT License
  https://github.com/devicons/devicon
    clickhouse.svg, mariadb.svg, mysql.svg, oracle.svg, postgresql.svg,
    spanner.svg, sqlite.svg, sqlserver.svg, yugabytedb.svg

  simple-icons/simple-icons 16.30.0, CC0 1.0 Universal
  https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons
    cockroachdb.svg

cockroachdb.svg is the only edited file: simple-icons ships its icons as a
single monochrome path, so the fill carries the brand's own hex (#6933FF) as
that project's metadata records it. Nine coloured marks beside one black one
would read as a distinction Ptah is not making.

